# Home Base edge sign-in
#
# Adds: trust the person the Home Base edge proxy signed in, via Authentik.
# Why: Home Base signs people in once, at the edge. The edge forwards each
# request with X-Home-Base-User, X-Home-Base-Groups, and a shared secret,
# X-Home-Base-Edge-Secret. When ODYSSEUS_EDGE_SECRET is set and the secret
# matches, compared in constant time, Odysseus treats that user as signed in
# and keeps the user for the rest of the request in src/home_base_identity.py.
# /api/auth/status reports the same user, since the front end asks it
# whether someone is signed in.
#
# Edge sign-in creates the account on first sight and marks it, and only ever
# maps onto accounts it created: an Authentik account named like a local
# Odysseus account, such as the bootstrap admin, is refused. Admin rights
# follow membership in the Authentik group HOME_BASE_ADMIN_GROUP (default
# home-base-admins) on every sign-in. Without the secret nothing changes, so
# other containers on the rack network cannot claim to be anyone.
# Upstream: a Home Base feature, not a bug fix. Not for upstream as is.
# Test: tests/test_home_base_identity.py

